WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.903
-As the FBI investigators
sexual-assault allegations

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.871
against Supreme Court nominee
Brett Kavanaugh,

00:00:05.871 --> 00:00:07.474
it's become clear
that he is very much

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:09.475
like the president
who nominated him.

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:11.911
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:16.615
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.615 --> 00:00:18.117
The Kavanaugh allegations,

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:20.019
perhaps more
than any other story,

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:22.688
have made Republicans
absolutely lose their minds.

00:00:22.688 --> 00:00:25.324
In the last week, we've seen a
nominee for the Supreme Court

00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:27.093
scream and cry
in a Senate hearing,

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:28.895
Senators threaten
their colleagues,

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:31.531
and the President gave multiple
rambling press conferences

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:34.733 line:0%
that were so incoherent, even
the closed captioning gave up.

00:00:34.733 --> 00:00:36.536 line:0%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:39.906
And one of the surest signs
that Trump is losing his mind

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:42.175
over the Kavanaugh crisis
is that he's accusing

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:44.811
everyone else of going crazy.

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:47.480
Trump always deflects criticism
by projecting onto others

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.315
whatever he's accused of,
and lately,

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:51.517
he's even adopted
a new catch phrase.

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:54.520
-They have been blind --
in a blind rage --

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:58.257
ever since, boy,
they lost the 2016 election.

00:00:58.257 --> 00:01:01.093
They've gone loco.

00:01:01.093 --> 00:01:02.795
They have gone loco.

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:04.530
These people,
they've gone crazy.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:05.898
They've gone loco.

00:01:05.898 --> 00:01:07.433
-When I won,
I said, "The good thing is

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:09.468
now the press finally gets it.

00:01:09.468 --> 00:01:12.271
Now they'll finally
treat me fairly."

00:01:12.271 --> 00:01:14.207
They got worse.

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:16.442
They're worse now than ever.

00:01:16.442 --> 00:01:18.378
They're loco.
But that's okay.

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:20.713
I put up with it.
Go ahead.

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:22.615
I use that word
because of the fact

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.683
that we made a deal with Mexico.

00:01:24.683 --> 00:01:27.053
-Oh, is that why?
[ Audience groans ]

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:28.354
Is that why you used it?

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:30.190
"We had meetings with Mexico,

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.958
and they were using
the word 'loco' a lot.

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:34.694
Apparently --"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.963
Apparently, it's their word
for 'president.'"

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:40.299
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:40.299 --> 00:01:44.871
Also, why does he point
to his head when he says loco?

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:47.039
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.039 --> 00:01:50.243
He can't even do
basic hand gestures right.

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:52.178
And what is this thing
he does all the time?

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:55.448
Just some jackass version
of jazz hands.

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:57.283
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.283 --> 00:02:00.219
Like he's dancing
next to Shirley Temple.

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:04.790
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:06.725
Trump reminds me
of an '80s movie

00:02:06.725 --> 00:02:08.394
where an alien
crash lands on Earth

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:10.362
and tries
to learn human culture.

00:02:10.362 --> 00:02:12.065
I'd love to see him
flip someone off.

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:14.334
"Hey, man, F you."

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:18.571
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:20.607
Trump is going loco,
because, in Kavanaugh,

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:22.442
he very much sees himself --
a powerful man

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:23.843
who's led a privileged life,

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:25.978
who's never before been held
accountable for his actions,

00:02:25.978 --> 00:02:28.081
suddenly being challenged
over his treatment of women.

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:30.316
In fact, yesterday,
Trump pretty much spelled it out

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:31.683
when he was asked
if he had a message

00:02:31.683 --> 00:02:33.085
for young men in America.

00:02:33.085 --> 00:02:35.255
-Well, I'd say that it's
a very scary time

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:38.791
for young men in America
when you can be

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:41.461
guilty of something
that you may not be guilty of.

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:43.963
Somebody could accuse you
of something,

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:45.832
and you're automatically guilty.

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:49.802
But in this realm, you are truly
guilty until proven innocent.

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:52.071
-Oh, you suddenly care
about due process

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:53.405
and the presumption
of innocence?

00:02:53.405 --> 00:02:55.608
Because when
you mention Hillary Clinton

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:57.543
at your most recent rally,

00:02:57.543 --> 00:03:00.013
your supporters
were still chanting this.

00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:07.253
No, I'm sure they meant to
chant, "Lock her up only after

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:09.122
a fair trail in which
overwhelming evidence

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:10.189
of wrongdoing is presented."

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:12.624
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:03:12.624 --> 00:03:16.629
I mean, obviously,
it's a little longer, but...

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:18.230
[ Applause ]

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:20.866
Also, it's so sad that they're
still chanting "Lock her up."

00:03:20.866 --> 00:03:22.535
Let it go.
Hillary's out there

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:24.137
selling books,
sipping Chardonnay,

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:26.005
and making cameos
on "Murphy Brown,"

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:29.208
and you guys are all crammed
into a local civic center,

00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:31.611
watching the world's
sweatiest man have an aneurysm.

00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:32.712
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:35.114
Kavanaugh's also lied repeatedly

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:36.883
about his heavy drinking
in high school and college days.

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:39.552
Trump was asked about that
and decided to talk instead

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:42.154
about his own decision
to abstain from alcohol.

00:03:42.154 --> 00:03:44.290
-Well, I don't drink.
I've never had a drink.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:47.359
I don't drink beer.
I've never had a beer.

00:03:47.359 --> 00:03:49.762
And I'm not saying good or bad.
Some people like it.

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:53.665
I just chose not to do that
for a lot of reasons.

00:03:53.665 --> 00:03:55.901
I think that...

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:58.838
I remember my college days.
Everybody was drinking.

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:02.041
It was like normal.
I was abnormal.

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:05.345
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
Yeah.

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:06.746
Yeah.

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:08.948
Yeah, we're aware of that.
We all know you're abnormal.

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:11.083
And "abnormal"
is the best word for Trump,

00:04:11.083 --> 00:04:14.152
because it's how you describe
a weird mole, you know?

00:04:14.152 --> 00:04:15.221
"What do you think, doc?"

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:16.522
"Well, it's definitely abnormal.

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:20.026
It's red, irritated, and all
the hair is falling out."

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:22.628
So Republicans have been
losing their minds

00:04:22.628 --> 00:04:24.463
over the Kavanaugh allegations,
and last night,

00:04:24.463 --> 00:04:27.466
Trump took his meltdown
to a new level -- openly mocking

00:04:27.466 --> 00:04:29.668
Dr. Christine Blasey Ford's
testimony

00:04:29.668 --> 00:04:31.537
at a rally in Mississippi.

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:34.206
-36 years ago, this happened.

00:04:34.206 --> 00:04:37.076
"I had one beer, right?

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:38.911
I had one beer."

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:40.313
"Well, you think it was --"

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:42.248
"No, it was one beer."
"Oh, good.

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:44.283
How did you get home?"
"I don't remember."

00:04:44.283 --> 00:04:45.685
"How'd you get there?"
"I don't remember."

00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:47.387
"Where is the place?"
"I don't remember."

00:04:47.387 --> 00:04:49.955
"How many years ago was it?"
"I don't know.

00:04:49.955 --> 00:04:52.358
I don't know."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:56.995
"I don't know.
I don't know."

00:04:56.995 --> 00:04:58.865
"What neighborhood was it in?"
"I don't know."

00:04:58.865 --> 00:05:01.467
"Where's the house?"
"I don't know."

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.402
"Upstairs, downstairs,
where was it?"

00:05:03.402 --> 00:05:04.870
"I don't know.
But I had one beer.

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:06.472
That's the only thing
I remember."

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:08.407
-I mean, that's the President
of the United States

00:05:08.407 --> 00:05:10.877
openly mocking a survivor
of sexual assault.

00:05:10.877 --> 00:05:12.411
There's no rock bottom
for this guy.

00:05:12.411 --> 00:05:15.014
Rock bottom
is where he jumped from.

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:16.782
And let this be a lesson --

00:05:16.782 --> 00:05:19.485
Let this be a lesson to everyone
who is praising Trump

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:22.187
for his supposedly
respectful handling of Dr. Ford.

00:05:22.187 --> 00:05:23.722
You knew this was coming.

00:05:23.722 --> 00:05:25.725
It's like a werewolf movie
where someone says,

00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:28.027
"He hasn't turned into a wolf
for 29 days,

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:29.595
so I think we're good."

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:31.163
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.163 --> 00:05:33.999
"Unlock his bedroom."

00:05:33.999 --> 00:05:35.501
Seriously, man,
what's wrong with you?

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:37.569
Look at him --
red-faced, sweaty.

00:05:37.569 --> 00:05:39.071
Trump's never
had a drink in his life,

00:05:39.071 --> 00:05:42.408
and somehow,
he's still an angry drunk.

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:43.876
And by the way,
your little re-enactment

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:45.578
of Ford's testimony
was wrong anyway.

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:47.079
Just because you
don't remember the details

00:05:47.079 --> 00:05:48.281
doesn't mean she didn't.

00:05:48.281 --> 00:05:50.149
Her testimony
under unimaginable trauma

00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:52.451
was searing and yet somehow
still incredibly composed.

00:05:52.451 --> 00:05:53.786
Meanwhile, if someone asked you

00:05:53.786 --> 00:05:55.354
one question
at a press conference,

00:05:55.354 --> 00:05:57.723
you melt down like you just saw
the Arc of the Covenant.

00:05:57.723 --> 00:05:59.525
-Should the FBI interview

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:02.227
all three of Brett Kavanaugh's
accusers?

00:06:02.227 --> 00:06:06.132
-Aaaaaaah!

00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:08.634
-And much like Kavanaugh...

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:10.402
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:10.402 --> 00:06:13.172
Much like Kavanaugh,

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:15.007
Trump has also repeatedly lied

00:06:15.007 --> 00:06:16.409
about the allegations
against him,

00:06:16.409 --> 00:06:18.210
like the hush payment
to Stormy Daniels

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:20.613
that Trump's personal fixer
Michael Cohen made

00:06:20.613 --> 00:06:22.381
in the closing days
of the campaign.

00:06:22.381 --> 00:06:23.949
Remember when Trump said he had

00:06:23.949 --> 00:06:25.384
absolutely nothing
to do with that payment,

00:06:25.384 --> 00:06:27.920
and then his lawyer went on TV
and said he did know

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:30.088
and then took it back
and said he didn't know,

00:06:30.088 --> 00:06:31.757
and then Trump said he did know

00:06:31.757 --> 00:06:34.460
and then said his lawyer
was wrong when he said he knew?

00:06:40.999 --> 00:06:43.136
-They funneled it
through a law firm.

00:06:43.136 --> 00:06:45.538
-Funneled through a law firm,
and the President repaid it.

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:48.040 line:0%
-Excuse me, excuse me,
excuse me.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:49.642 line:0%
No, but you have to --

00:06:49.642 --> 00:06:51.243 line:0%
Excuse me.
You take a look at what I said.

00:06:51.243 --> 00:06:53.379
You go back and take a look.
You'll see what I said.

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:57.283 line:0%
You go take a look
at what we said.

00:06:57.283 --> 00:06:58.718
-Yeah, dude.

00:06:58.718 --> 00:07:02.054
You were asked if you knew about
the payment, and you said no.

00:07:02.054 --> 00:07:03.623
We saw it, remember?

00:07:03.623 --> 00:07:05.491
You were standing
in the aisle of the plane

00:07:05.491 --> 00:07:08.360
like you were about to take
everyone's drink orders.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:09.929
"Oh, I'll just have a snack."

00:07:09.929 --> 00:07:11.964
"We don't have snacks."
"You just said you did."

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:13.432
"Go back and take a look
at what I said."

00:07:13.432 --> 00:07:14.934
[ Laughter ]

00:07:14.934 --> 00:07:17.770
Then, of course, it turned out
that Trump was directly involved

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:19.238
in the payment,
and then, on Tuesday,

00:07:19.238 --> 00:07:21.974
we found out that, in February,
while he was President,

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:25.244
Trump had personally sought
to keep Stormy Daniels quiet.

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:27.212
-A source with direct knowledge
tells CNN

00:07:27.212 --> 00:07:29.481
President Trump
personally directed an effort

00:07:29.481 --> 00:07:31.918
to keep porn star
Stormy Daniels quiet

00:07:31.918 --> 00:07:35.988
about a sexual encounter she
says she had with him in 2006.

00:07:35.988 --> 00:07:38.557
In February, the President
called his now former

00:07:38.557 --> 00:07:40.993
personal attorney Michael Cohen
and instructed him

00:07:40.993 --> 00:07:43.362
to seek a restraining order
against Daniels.

00:07:43.362 --> 00:07:45.164
The source says
Trump directed Cohen

00:07:45.164 --> 00:07:47.732
to coordinate the effort
involving his son, Eric Trump,

00:07:47.732 --> 00:07:49.134
and an outside lawyer.

00:07:49.134 --> 00:07:51.170
-You put Eric on the case?

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:52.905
[ Laughter ]

00:07:52.905 --> 00:07:55.241
I'm not surprised
the cover-up failed.

00:07:55.241 --> 00:07:57.643
I'm surprised we didn't end up
with video from three angles

00:07:57.643 --> 00:07:59.211
and a signed confession.

00:07:59.211 --> 00:08:00.580
[ Laughter ]

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:02.348
So, to recap,
Trump personally intervened

00:08:02.348 --> 00:08:04.216
to keep a porn star
from speaking publicly

00:08:04.216 --> 00:08:05.951
about an affair
he illegally covered up

00:08:05.951 --> 00:08:07.452
during a presidential campaign,

00:08:07.452 --> 00:08:10.356
and he put his
two dumbest subordinates on it.

00:08:10.356 --> 00:08:11.790
Although, in fairness,
it's not like

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:13.792
Trump's surrounded by geniuses.

00:08:13.792 --> 00:08:15.461
"We need to stop
this Stormy thing.

00:08:15.461 --> 00:08:17.330
Who's the smartest guy here?

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:20.165
Me?
Oh. That's not good."

00:08:20.165 --> 00:08:21.867
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:21.867 --> 00:08:25.338
These guys lie --
They lie to hold on to power

00:08:25.338 --> 00:08:26.639
because they think
they're entitled to it.

00:08:26.639 --> 00:08:28.841
That's why they're all furious
and indignant

00:08:28.841 --> 00:08:30.042
when you question them
in any way.

00:08:30.042 --> 00:08:32.011
If you suggest that they
broke the law

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:33.779
to become president
or they shouldn't sit

00:08:33.779 --> 00:08:35.748
on the Supreme Court,
they go absolutely...

00:08:35.748 --> 00:08:37.016
-Loco.

00:08:37.016 --> 00:08:38.384
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:08:38.384 --> 00:08:42.221
[ Cheers and applause ]

